1 OCCU домакиня, Húsfreyja í Víðidalstungu - síðar fylgikona Sigmundar, Húsfreyja í Víðidalstungu, síðar á Breiðabólsstað í Vesturhópi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Íslendingabók:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sólveig Þorleifsdóttir   Fædd um 1415  Látin 1479  Húsfreyja í Víðidalstungu, síðar á Breiðabólsstað í Vesturhópi.  Heimildir: Ísl. ættstuðlar, Esp.4942, Ann.I.58, N. KÁ/GF 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Solveig Thorleifsdottir married Ormur (Worm) Loftsson from Hjardarholt (son of Loftur Gudormssonar) from Modru Vollum.  Solveig's father-in-law Loftur was the richest man of his time, powerful and an intellect and poet.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Solveig got tangled with an alcoholic bum - a priest by the name of Sigmund Steindorsson from Mikla-Bae.   She had 5 children with him and from there followed a big ancestral lineage of prominent citizens in Icelandic society.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Ormur divorced Solveig and left her a big share of his wealth.   He died in 1446.   When Solveig and Sigmund's son Jon Sigmundssn inherited his mother's wealth Bishop Olafur Rognvaldson rose up and put in a claim to all the money 
2 CONC and property for the church in Skalholt.
