2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Bengt Algotsson's ancestral family. The darkness that has long rested over King Magnus Eriksson's favorite, the family of the well-known Duke Bengt Algotsson, has in recent decades begun to dissipate. It has been shown that h
2 CONC e was far from being of low birth, as previously claimed, belonged to one of Sweden's most high-born families, and that through his grandmother Mrs. Ingegärd Svantepolksdotter he could lead his family up to both the Sverker royal 
2 CONC family and the Danish King Valdemar Sejer.1 On the other hand, the father has not been able to trace his lineage further back than to his grandfather Brynjulf ​​Bengtsson, who is mentioned in the Nordic Family Book. . Then, howeve
2 CONC r, nothing but the common weapon image, the lion, speaks for this assumption and also Bengt Magnusson's family was attached to Östergötland, but Duke Bengts again at Vestergötland, one should be fully entitled to throw this whole 
2 CONC derivation over the table as less likely, if at the same time a more acceptable family management can be demonstrated. Duke Bengt, his father Algot Brynjulfsson, uncle Knut Brynjulfsson and aunts Birgitta Brynjulfsdotter, gm the k
2 CONC night Greger Magnusson (2 slanted beams), and Katarina Brynjulfsdotter gm the knight Ulf Håkansson (Läma), carried a lion in the shield, and then the lion image of Vest lagmannen Bengt Haf- 1 Illustrated Swedish history 2, p. 24. 
2 CONC one should be fully entitled to throw this whole derivation over the table as less likely, if at the same time a more plausible lineage can be demonstrated. Duke Bengt, his father Algot Brynjulfsson, uncle Knut Brynjulfsson and au
2 CONC nts Birgitta Brynjulfsdotter, gm the knight Greger Magnusson (2 slanted beams), and Katarina Brynjulfsdotter gm the knight Ulf Håkansson (Läma), carried a lion in the shield, and then the lion image of Vest lagmannen Bengt Haf- 1 
2 CONC Illustrated Swedish history 2, p. 24. one should be fully entitled to throw this whole derivation over the table as less likely, if at the same time a more plausible lineage can be demonstrated. Duke Bengt, his father Algot Brynju
2 CONC lfsson, uncle Knut Brynjulfsson and aunts Birgitta Brynjulfsdotter, gm the knight Greger Magnusson (2 slanted beams), and Katarina Brynjulfsdotter gm the knight Ulf Håkansson (Läma), carried a lion in the shield, and then the lion
2 CONC  image of Vest lagmannen Bengt Haf- 1 Illustrated Swedish history 2, p. 24. och då lejonbilden äfven föres af Vestgöta-lagmannen Bengt Haf- 1 Illustrerad Svensk historia 2, sid. 24. och då lejonbilden äfven föres af Vestgöta-lagma
2 CONC nnen Bengt Haf- 1 Illustrerad Svensk historia 2, sid. 24.
