1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 32562. Arnbjørn* ÅMUNDSSON Ile(765) (908)(909) (827)(767) was born about 1505 in Ile gård #31, Vikedal, Rogaland, Norway. He died after 1575 in Ile gård #31, Vikedal, Rogaland, Norway. Arnbjørn Åmundsson was first 
2 CONC named in a lawsuit over the allodial rights to Vaula in Mosterøy. He was named as a lagrettemann in a document from 1575 and also described as previously being the first lensmann in Ile, Vats and a "distinguished and wise man". In
2 CONC  1563 Arnbjørn paid a tax of 6 lodd silver and 18 shillings on his estate. That would indicate that his taxable real estate was worth 6 or 7 laupar smør. Since he lived tax free at Ile (worth about 3 laupar smør), his total estate
2 CONC  in 1563 would have been about 10 laupar smør.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 16281 
2 CONT
2 CONT i. [?, wife of Åsmund Eriksson] ARNBJØRNSDATTER Ile. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. Åmund ARNBJØRNSSON Ile(827) (767) was born about 1530 in Vikedal, Rogaland, Norway. He died about 1603 in Ile gård #31, Vikedal, Rogaland, Norway. Åmund Arnbjørnsson was one of the lagrettemenn who signed the credentials of th
2 CONC e representatives from Vats who attended the 1591 coronation in Oslo. He was also one of five men in Vats who paid tax as a large landowner. His wife's name might have been Ragnhild, but that is not certain.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Han var den første lensmannen man kjenner til i det gamle Vats skiprede, og han var lagrettemann i 1578. Han bodde da på Ile i Vikedal. Arnbjørn Amundsen Ihle er nevnt første gang i 1554 i en odelsak på Vaula i Mosterøy. Der sies 
2 CONC det at han er bror til hr. Trugils (Torgils) Amundsen (kannik i Stavanger og abbed i Utstein kloster). (Slektene Velde og Espeland og inngiftede slekter. s. 21-23.)
