1 NOTE Wiki Link
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=cb7f840c-d992-4298-980f-c2229f8635ec&tid=19589623&pid=835474053
1 NOTE During the struggle for the throne of Norway in the 12th centure Sverrir of the Faroe Islands, who claimed to be the son of Sigurd Munn, claimed the throne about 1175, and ruled until 1202.
1 NOTE     * OCCUPATION: Konge i Norge 1177-1202
2 CONT     * BIRTH: 1152, (Sverker) (Neppe sønn av Sigurd Munn) Færøene ?
2 CONT     * BAPTISM: "Sverre prest"
2 CONT     * DEATH: 9 Mar 1202, Bergen 
2 CONT
2 CONT Han talte Roma midt i mot!
1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT King of Norway 1184-1202.  Reunified Norway 1184.  Ordained priest.
2 CONT His mother claimed he was son of Sigurd II.  Faeroes > Norway 1174 to claim
2 CONT throne.  Became king in Trondheim 1179. Excommunicated 1194 (for assertion
2 CONT of royal power to elect bishops).  Church waged war against him 1196-1202.
2 CONT nygols gives Astrid Roesd. as his mother, not wife -- all others agree she
2 CONT is wife.
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT http://home.sol.no/~nermo/slekt/d0005/g0000002.html#I1483
2 CONT EB(1980) v. IX, p. 706
2 CONT Library of Univeral History v. 6 p. 1858
2 CONT http://www.norske.org/family/ghtout/gp270.htm
