1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/db10061511254227 Publikasjoner utgitt av Arkivverket, PUBL/PUBL-001/C/0003: Bind 3: Skatten av Bergenhus len 1563, 1563, s. 19] (Halffparttenn aff all jordeigende bønders landschyld
2 CONC tt aff Jerenn och Dalerne: anno 1563: Thorleiff på Orsta)
2 CONT * [https://www.nb.no/items/7030d184bbc50ed3e1dac0748f60b679?page=211 "Hetland skipsreide i 450 år: Bind 1. Heskestad sokn: Gard, ætt og folk" (Grøsfjell, 3. Tollak Asserson Grøsfjell, p. 202)]
2 CONT * [https://www.nb.no/items/7030d184bbc50ed3e1dac0748f60b679?page=211 "Hetland skipsreide i 450 år: Bind 1. Heskestad sokn: Gard, ætt og folk" (Grøsfjell, 1. Asser Grøsfjell, p. 202)]
2 CONT * [https://www.nb.no/items/876d3c181419a05b42a5169800396780?page=312 "Hetland skipsreide i 450 år: Bind 2. Helleland sokn: Gard, ætt og folk" (Hesvik, 1. Tollak Asserson (Grøsfjell), p. 303)]
2 CONT * [https://www.nb.no/items/9f3df5c0d3cee86a23f30408ef31446c?page=126 "Gards og Ættesoga for Ogna" (Kvalbein, 8. Peder Rasmusson Kvalbein, pp. 123-126)]
2 CONT * [https://www.nb.no/items/5f0e4a8385ea53c3e2060bf36a7ced11?page=62 P. Valand, 1960, "Manges opphav i Dalane. Corrigenda et Addenda" (IX. Årstad-Tengs i Eigersund), ''Ætt og Heim'', pp. 61-66]
2 CONT * [https://www.nb.no/items/49a8feacccdac4dbc4e1052c4bd159d3?page=44 P. Valand, 1963, "Fortiden dukker fram i dagen. Hvem eide Orrestad i Helleland 1555", ''Ætt og Heim'', pp. 39-41]
2 CONT * [https://www.nb.no/items/27bac5facc236bf627db70dff717fa64?page=111 P. Valand, 1964, "Gamle ætter i Dalane. Corrigenda & Addenda III", ''Ætt og Heim'', pp. 110-121]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT The parentage of the Tollak Grøsfjell that is mentioned in 1567 is not known for sure. Some contributors here at Geni, and elsewhere claim that he is ''the same person as'' Tollak Assersen Grøsfjell. This seems highly unlikely, an
2 CONC d may be based on a misreading of secondary sources. The main authority on Heskestad/Helleland, Petrus Valand, [https://www.nb.no/items/5f0e4a8385ea53c3e2060bf36a7ced11?page=66 speculated in 1960] that the 'Tollak Grøsfjell', ment
2 CONC ioned in 1567, may have been a son of Torkel Tollaksen Heltand, mentioned in 1563, who himself was a son of Tollak Assersen Grøsfjell, mentioned in 1521, and his first unknown wife, who held allodial rights at Skadberg farm. Just 
2 CONC three years later, [https://www.nb.no/items/49a8feacccdac4dbc4e1052c4bd159d3?page=45 in 1963], the same Petrus Valand, speculated that the 'Tollak (Tollaksen?) Grøsfjell', mentioned in 1567, may have been a ''son of'' Tollak Asser
2 CONC sen Grøsfjell. Eight years thereafter, in [https://www.nb.no/items/7030d184bbc50ed3e1dac0748f60b679?page=211 "Heskestad sokn: Gard, ætt og folk"], Petrus Valand stated that the Tollak Grøsfjell that is mentioned in 1567 was most l
2 CONC ikely a ''grandson of'' Tollak Assersen Grøsfjell. In neither of these cases does Peder Valand suggest that the 'Tollak Grøsfjell' that is mentioned in 1567 was ''identical to'' Tollak Assersen Grøsfjell. The latter theory seems t
2 CONC o be the most plausible one, but as only one son of Tollak Assersen Grøsfjell is known, it seems most likely (but in no way proved) that the patronym of the Tollak Grøsfjell that is mentioned in 1567 was "Torkelsen".
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 NOTE Roald Undheims notater s.58 og 35. Heskestad, Dybing 110.1. Egersund/Helleland, Strømstad 837. Ætt&Heim 1964 s.113.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 CONT Navnet er skrevet Tollef, men Tollef og Tollak brukes om hverandre og barna hans har Tollaknavn. Gift med Ingeleiv Ormsdtr. Årstad. Born:
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 CONT a. N.N. Tollaksdtr. (se denne), g.m. Jakob Dybing, Heskestad.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 CONT b. Helga Tollaksdtr. (se denne) g.m. presten Olav Jonson i Egersund.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 CONT c. Endre Tollakson, Årstad 1591.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 CONT d. Laurits Tollakson (se denne) Store Ege i 1563 - 1602.
2 CONT
