1 CONC lly wounded in the same fight. Marg aret, we are told, died soon after receiving the news of their deaths . The Annals of Ulster say:
1 CONT
1 CONT Mael Coluim son of Donnchad, over-king of Scotland, and Edward his son , were killed by the French i.e. in Inber Alda in England. His queen,M argaret, moreover, died of sorrow for him within nine days. Máel Colui m's body was take
1 CONC n to Tynemouth for burial. It may later have been reb uried at Dunfermline Abbey in the reign of his son Alexander or perhap s on Iona.
